#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:177
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`No` when there is no event file, the event carries no issue with an author, or the layer has no declaration to resolve its translations directory from. That is \"could not determine\" (exit 2): the run fails, and it is never read as \"nothing to record\"."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:245
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`No`: the PR is closed and nothing is recorded; the issue stays as the account of what was asked. `Yes`: the records are in the repository."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`translation:adjudicate` reads the `issues` event GitHub wrote, never the body from a shell variable: the body is untrusted and is only parsed as JSON. It decides every write before making any, and refuses rather than guesses."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:109
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`translation:status` writes `review.html` beside the status page, with `assets/translation-status/review.json`: every catalogue × locale, its state (`machine`, `flagged`, `reviewed`, `stale`, `official`), the candidates per string, and the hash of the catalogue's bytes. That hash is what the verdict is pinned to."
msgstr ""

