#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A person's verdict on a machine translation, carried from the review page to the record. Candidate translations come from any engine; a reviewer accepts what is there, or flags a mistranslation and picks a candidate or writes their own; the verdict travels as a GitHub issue; a workflow checks it and opens a pull request; a maintainer merges it. You are in this process when a catalogue has a translation nobody has adjudicated: a `machine`, `flagged` or `stale` cell on the review page. `translation-workflow` produces the machine translation and `human-translation-workflow` makes a locale official; this process sits between them and does neither. What it records is that ONE catalogue was read by ONE person who could be held to it, against the exact bytes they saw. Two rules hold throughout. Candidates are never a barrier to having a translation: an empty `msgstr` gets the first candidate, marked fuzzy, so the page always has something to show. And a suggestion is a person's text that nobody else has reviewed: it enters the catalogue fuzzy, flagging it for review, never accepting it. Locale sign-off (`X-Folio-Official`, the locale's `status.json`) is a separate, deliberate act that this process never performs. GitHub is one Tool here, not the process: the issue is the carrier of the verdict and the pull request the carrier of the record. Another forge carrying the same `translation-adjudication/v1` record would be another Tool satisfying the same skill."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:280
#. Diagram label
msgid "Acceptable"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:216
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Acceptable: the catalogue's translation node gets `signedOffBy` / `signedOffAt`. Mistranslation: each suggestion replaces its `msgstr`, marked `#, fuzzy`. Either way an entry is appended to the catalogue's `translation-qa` attestation (criterion `human-adjudication`) naming the issue and the hash the person saw; the attestation is append-only and checked against `qa-attestations/v1` before it is written. The PO header `X-Folio-Official` and the locale's `status.json` are never touched."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:128
#. Diagram label
msgid "Acceptable?"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:299
#. Diagram label
msgid "Accepted"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Accepts the record into the repository, or does not. The maintainer judges whether the PR records what the issue asked, not the translation itself: that was the reviewer's verdict, and merging does not re-make it. A PR opened by the workflow starts no other workflows, so the layer's checks run once the maintainer pushes to it or re-opens it."
msgstr ""

