#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One or more candidate sources write alternatives per string to `translations/<locale>/<catalogue>.candidates.json` (`translation-candidates/v1`), each candidate carrying its source: an agent model, an open machine-translation model, a web service, or a person. The engines are interchangeable behind one skill, `translation-candidate-source`: whichever runs, the same sidecar comes out. Writers append; a candidate is never a verdict."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:224
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open a ready PR and comment"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:129
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Per catalogue, the reviewer's verdict. `Acceptable`: the translation as it stands. `Mistranslation`: one or more strings are wrong, and the reviewer says what they should be."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:195
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Per item: is the catalogue's hash today the one the page showed, does its path stay inside the translations directory, and is every suggestion's `current` text still what the catalogue says? An item that fails is refused with its reason (reload the page and review it again). `No` when every item is refused; `Yes` when at least one survives, and the refusals are reported beside what was recorded."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Per string: does the `.po` have no translation for a string the engine just gave candidates for? `Yes` seeds it. `No` leaves the `.po` alone: an existing translation is not replaced by a candidate, only offered beside it."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:135
#. Diagram label
msgid "Pick a candidate or write your own"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Plan the records (translation:adjudicate)"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:76
#. Diagram label
msgid "Produce candidate translations (any engine)"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:188
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read from the event's `author_association`, never from the body. `No`: nothing is recorded, and the comment says a maintainer can file the same review under their own name. A record that does not parse, or that names another repository or another translations directory, is refused at this point too."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:119
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the catalogue on the review page"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:235
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review the PR; merge or close"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer (adjudicator)"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:145
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Submit opens GitHub's new-issue form prefilled with a readable summary and a `translation-adjudication/v1` JSON block, labelled `translation-adjudication` and titled `[translation review] …`. When the record is too long for a URL the page copies the body for pasting instead. Filing it is the act of adjudicating."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:300
#. Diagram label
msgid "Suggestion applied"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:236
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The maintainer checks that the PR writes down what the issue decided and nothing else, lets the layer's checks run, and merges or closes it."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only lane that judges a translation. The person who files the issue IS the adjudicator: their GitHub login is the only identity the record carries, and nothing they type in the body can name anyone else. Choosing a candidate is a judgement too, so the candidate's source is recorded with the verdict."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:263
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The review page shows the catalogue `reviewed`, and `stale` once its bytes change. It is still not official: locale sign-off is `human-translation-workflow`'s `Task_Signoff`, a separate act by the translation coordinator."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer opens the review page and reads one catalogue's strings against their source, with the candidates beside each."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:268
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The suggestions are in the catalogue, fuzzy, so the catalogue needs review again: a person's text is not reviewed by being written. The next review is a new instance of this process."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:157
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The workflow runs for an issue that is labelled or titled as an adjudication, and once per issue: `Yes` when the issue's branch already exists, and nothing more is done."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:16
#. Diagram label
msgid "Translation review and adjudication"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two fixed programs and no judgement: the candidate engines and the page generator before the review, the adjudication workflow after it. Every refusal on the right of this lane is the workflow declining to guess, and each says why on the issue. It never merges and never signs a locale off."
msgstr ""

